These possibilities provide
a set of criteria for describing the semantic structure of a given vocabulary:

* (1) The dosage of motivated and unmotivated words;
* (2) The dosage of particular and generic terms;
* (3) Special devices for conveying emotive overtones;
* (4) The organization and distribution of synonymic resources;
* (5) The relative frequency of polysemy; its characteristic forms; safeguards against ambiguities to which it may give rise;
* (6) The relative frequency of homonymy; safeguards against conflicts between homonyms.

